#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572274} :activity/id #uuid "4ca754f9-66ec-57c4-90b0-89b0d470c805" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159 :topic/id #uuid "df2bac79-2def-521c-b3f0-baba942d57fa" :topic/math-academy-id 1771} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572229 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4f377f6-a622-5fb1-83fd-b51ffde95279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448374} {:answer/id #uuid "e8eef12c-f75a-57eb-864c-4e964e2546ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448375} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a710d21-aa98-556e-bce1-7285a2958cab" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449227} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19290501-5f97-5824-a9af-b80c15fcba75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448376} {:answer/id #uuid "32b6d299-66b2-5419-ac6b-a58da54978bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448377}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448376} :answer-field/id #uuid "cabaddcb-b811-5980-9f7e-c9abd629060e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f97bf8ab-3778-53a9-b3ca-2e0bcc162bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448378} {:answer/id #uuid "9176f6a5-fa1c-5b16-8ef6-dac388fbaa52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448379}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448379} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6b06da-5269-50f6-bb62-acb18d224336" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dcce1957-fa55-5f89-a722-cbd09d149dbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-130364" :question/problem "Given that $det({A}^{T})=7$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3\\text{det}(A)=21$\n- **II.** $-2\\text{det}({A}^{T})=14$\n- **III.** $\\text{det}(A)+2\\text{det}(I)=9$" :question/worked-solution "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)=\\text{det}({A}^{T})=7\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3\\text{det}(A)=3\\cdot 7=21.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n-2\\text{det}({A}^{T})=-2\\cdot 7=-14\\ne 14.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)+2\\text{det}(I)=7+2\\cdot 1=9.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} :step/id #uuid "53a19a3f-7183-5af9-b4ef-496541e95b0f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572246}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572232 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e51492-c3b7-54b6-8660-3327203595bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272699} {:answer/id #uuid "28eeb732-2c18-5922-b6a9-bbd2d7eec5d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "480" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272751} {:answer/id #uuid "3084793d-d7d4-5080-9297-c5dbc7fc686c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272817} {:answer/id #uuid "b981ba03-1c73-5fee-958e-9f516f79590f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273996} {:answer/id #uuid "ed17d628-c951-506b-b286-13e3eb6a5ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274483}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272699} :answer-field/id #uuid "56164ca7-3d80-5b0c-bf3e-27409397895a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c594e512-d19a-53c5-8f50-4caaf295111c" :question/math-academy-id "q-158368" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,c=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $3$rd column of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =3\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-120|=120.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "59d231e0-c609-5e56-9c9c-328f2b57b9ad"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572246 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27aa8c33-edfb-5fb2-adfb-8de8ec26ee80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272737} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9e26c9-c473-5f4d-8f65-9bd62434b33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273182} {:answer/id #uuid "b6bc95c5-7da6-5228-b9f8-40a00f91ebed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273968} {:answer/id #uuid "bd7acf39-2806-5c1f-bac9-2f76b89d98e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274027} {:answer/id #uuid "dc81e9da-6f65-5e19-8784-3030b7eb61ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274324}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186274324} :answer-field/id #uuid "1470b275-7731-546d-9f3e-40a3009a30fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "edcd069d-5898-5a9f-9b4f-3515e782b5c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-158106" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,c=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=3\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot (-2)=-72.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-72|=72.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8328d6e8-8780-52d4-8262-9e63e4126b15" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572232}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572270 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9f7acf-4772-524d-9933-4e4b011382eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263101} {:answer/id #uuid "84991aa5-a164-5887-9901-28536fb438f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264138} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf8ec22-38b5-5754-a41d-3642a684daa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264466} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fd14d4-5f8d-53a4-85a5-f268e7755565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264882} {:answer/id #uuid "f3caa275-2457-5ac1-9efb-eeb0208aa29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265140}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264138} :answer-field/id #uuid "21720e07-443d-5bb2-ab55-5c097e6b5435" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9e66bdd6-8cff-5caf-91ee-00562039faba" :question/math-academy-id "q-130292" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $3$rd column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot 5\\cdot 6\\cdot (-1)=-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(B)=-60.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d8800461-b3c6-5776-8372-3b7d1884ef0d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572229}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572274 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a3d5b37-6c2a-5cba-ad78-e9a2626168b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571558} {:answer/id #uuid "593caf3a-5a8a-5474-911c-e4672c977ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571695} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa48bd6-79d0-527f-843f-9ca1892f691d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571697} {:answer/id #uuid "5e28842e-a45a-5471-b0f2-624733f6c02e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571702} {:answer/id #uuid "eca12e3d-3b57-505b-bd5b-c92cf39819a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571953}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571702} :answer-field/id #uuid "72d0d37d-2da5-57c2-b260-86d1c7a8fa86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1d6c75b7-d9d1-5c4f-a63e-3df78db605e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-42946" :question/problem "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$N=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the $1$st row contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(N) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{vmatrix} & =2\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{5})=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\ndet(N)=-10.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f07d655a-f0e9-5514-8478-5f380dc84331" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572270}}] :activity/title "Basic Properties of Determinants" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571523}]}
